# WN22-UR-000160: Windows Server 2022 lock pages in memory user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-ur-000160-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 lock pages in memory user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.`
    description `Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities. The "Lock pages in memory" user right allows physical memory to be assigned to processes, which could cause performance issues or a denial of service. Satisfies: SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125, SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00193`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,user-rights,security-policy,ksi-cna-mat,ksi-iam-jit,ksi-piy-rsd`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI:KSI-IAM-JIT,KSI:KSI-PIY-RSD,NIST-800-53:AC-6(10),NIST-800-53:SI-16`
    control_objective `KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI-IAM-JIT,KSI-PIY-RSD`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> User Rights Assignment >> Lock pages in memory to be defined but containing no entries (blank).`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_CNA_MAT `Windows Server implements KSI-CNA-MAT by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeLockMemoryPrivilege user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_JIT `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-JIT by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeLockMemoryPrivilege user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_PIY_RSD `Windows Server implements KSI-PIY-RSD by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeLockMemoryPrivilege user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_AC_6_10 `Windows Server implements AC-6(10) by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeLockMemoryPrivilege user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_SI_16 `Windows Server implements SI-16 by ensuring no accounts are granted the SeLockMemoryPrivilege user right. The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `SeLockMemoryPrivilege`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE absent
        exists boolean = false
    STATE_END

    STATE empty_list
        exists boolean = true
        member_count int = 0
    STATE_END

    CRI OR
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF absent
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF empty_list
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
